%C - SMBus Block Utility.
Execute DCMD_SMBUS_CMD devctl with the following commands:
    - SMBUS_CMD_BLOCK (n-byte payload)
    - SMBUS_CMD_I2C_READ (n-byte payload)


Usage:

%C -a address [-l length] [-n bus_path] [-v[v...]]
        [--i2c-en] [--i2c-read] [--pec] [--raw] [data]...


Options:

-a address, --addr=address
    Set the 7-bit slave address

-l length, --len=length
    Set the number of bytes to receive
    (default: 0)

-n bus_path, --path=bus_path
    Specify the location of the SMBus resource manger to attach to
    (default: /dev/smb0)

-v[v[v...]], --verbose=<level>
    Set the verbosity level of displayed details
    (default: 0)

--i2c-en
    Enable the I2C mode of the SMBus controller
    (default: disabled)

--i2c-read
    Force a read transaction with the SMBus command SMBUS_CMD_I2C_READ
    (default: SMBUS_CMD_BLOCK)

--pec
    Enable the Packet Error Code (PEC) feature
    (default: disabled)

--raw
    Display the received bytes as unformatted output
    (default: disabled)

data
    Specify the bytes to send


Examples:

- Read 5 bytes of SMBus device 0x40 (SMBUS_CMD_BLOCK)
%C -a 0x40 -l 5 0x00

- Write the byte sequence 0xDDCCBBAA in SMBus device 0x40 (SMBUS_CMD_BLOCK)
%C -a 0x40 0x4 0xAA 0xBB 0xCC 0xDD

- Write the byte sequence 0xDDCCBBAA in I2C device 0x44 (SMBUS_CMD_BLOCK)
%C -a 0x44 --i2c-en 0x4 0xAA 0xBB 0xCC 0xDD

- Read 256 byte starting at offset 0x00 of I2C device 0x50 (SMBUS_CMD_I2C_READ)
%C -a 0x50 --i2c-read -l 256 0x00
